{"t":{"t":10,"i":0,"p":{"k":["result","context"],"v":[{"t":10,"i":1,"p":{"k":["type","title","description","props"],"v":[{"t":1,"s":"openapi"},{"t":1,"s":"Create Prepaid Usage Addon"},{"t":1,"s":"Creates a prepaid usage addon definition under the specified product lineup. A prepaid addon can then be added and “provisioned” for a subscription.\\n\\nPrepaid addons allow customers to pre-purchase units that can be used up over time on their subscription. In a sense, they are the mirror image of metered addons; while metered addons charge at the end of the period for the amount of units used, prepaid addons are charged for at the time of purchase, and we subsequently keep track of the usage against the amount purchased.\\n\\nFor more information on addons, see our documentation here.\\n\\nIf you have the new Catalog experience enabled, taxable addons must include a non-blank `tax_code`. Sending `\\\"tax_code\\\": \\\"\\\"` returns `422`."},{"t":10,"i":2,"p":{"k":["payload","document","operations","showDescription"],"v":[{"t":10,"i":3,"p":{"k":["bundled","proxyUrl"],"v":[{"t":10,"i":4,"p":{"k":["openapi","info","tags","servers","security","paths","components"],"v":[{"t":1,"s":"3.2.0"},{"t":10,"i":5,"p":{"k":["title","version","contact","description","x-server-configuration"],"v":[{"t":1,"s":"Ombrevix Billing"},{"t":1,"s":"1.0"},{"t":10,"i":6,"p":{"k":["email"],"v":[{"t":1,"s":"support@ombrevix.example"}]},"o":0},{"t":1,"s":"\\nOmbrevix Billing provides an HTTP-based API that conforms to the principles of REST.\\nOne of the many reasons to use Ombrevix Billing is the immense feature set and client libraries.\\nThe Ombrevix API returns JSON responses as the primary and recommended format, but XML is also provided as a backwards compatible option for merchants who require it.\\n\\n## Steps to make your first Ombrevix Billing API call\\n\\n1. Sign-up or log-in to your test workspace account.\\n2. Setup authentication credentials.\\n3. Submit an API request and verify the response.\\n5. Test the Ombrevix Billing integrations.\\n\\nNext, you can explore authentication methods, basic concepts for interacting with Ombrevix Billing via the API, and the entire set of application-based documentation to aid in your discovery of the product.\\n\\n### Request Example\\n\\nThe following example uses the curl command-line tool to make an API request.\\n\\n**Request**\\n\\n    curl -u \\x3Capi_key>:x -H Accept:application/json -H Content-Type:application/json https://acme.ombrevix.example/subscriptions"},{"t":10,"i":7,"p":{"k":["default-server","default-environment","environments","parameters"],"v":[{"t":1,"s":"production"},{"t":1,"s":"US"},{"t":9,"i":8,"a":[{"t":10,"i":9,"p":{"k":["name","description","servers"],"v":[{"t":1,"s":"US"},{"t":1,"s":"Default Ombrevix Billing environment hosted in US. Valid for the majority of our customers."},{"t":9,"i":10,"a":[{"t":10,"i":11,"p":{"k":["url","name"],"v":[{"t":1,"s":"https://{workspace}.ombrevix.example"},{"t":1,"s":"production"}]},"o":0},{"t":10,"i":12,"p":{"k":["url","name"],"v":[{"t":1,"s":"https://events.ombrevix.example/{workspace}"},{"t":1,"s":"ebb"}]},"o":0},{"t":10,"i":13,"p":{"k":["url","name"],"v":[{"t":1,"s":"https://{connector}.api.ombrevix.example"},{"t":1,"s":"oauth"}]},"o":0}],"o":0}]},"o":0},{"t":10,"i":14,"p":{"k":["name","description","servers"],"v":[{"t":1,"s":"EU"},{"t":1,"s":"Ombrevix Billing environment hosted in EU. Use only when you requested EU hosting for your AB account."},{"t":9,"i":15,"a":[{"t":10,"i":16,"p":{"k":["url","name"],"v":[{"t":1,"s":"https://{workspace}.eu.ombrevix.example"},{"t":1,"s":"production"}]},"o":0},{"t":10,"i":17,"p":{"k":["url","name"],"v":[{"t":1,"s":"https://{connector}.api.ombrevix.example"},{"t":1,"s":"oauth"}]},"o":0}],"o":0}]},"o":0},{"t":10,"i":18,"p":{"k":["name","description","servers"],"v":[{"t":1,"s":"Ombrevix API Gateway"},{"t":1,"s":"Access Ombrevix Billing through a Ombrevix API Gateway connector. Authenticate with your connector Bearer to